## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, scalable moderation system design balancing latency, privacy, explainability, and governance across multilingual environments with live policy updates and comprehensive auditability.

## Key Concepts

- On-device vs cloud inference and data locality
- Policy-as-code with versioning and hot-reload capabilities
- Counterfactual explanations for decision transparency
- Privacy-preserving updates and tenant isolation
- Drift detection and comprehensive auditing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: update policy without redeploy
function updatePolicy(config) {
  const policyEngine = new PolicyAsCodeEngine();
  policyEngine.loadConfiguration(config);
  return policyEngine.validateCurrentRules();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical, latency-constrained, multilingual sarcasm detection with code-switching—common in global chat platforms.

## Key Concepts
- On-device inference for latency
- Code-switch aware tokenization
- Privacy-preserving learning (federated or DP-SGD)
- Drift detection and controlled rollouts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo on-device inference snippet
function inferSarcasm(text, model) {
  const tokens = codeSwitchTokenize(text);
  const emb = model.encode(tokens);
  const score = model.classify(emb);
  return score;
}
```

